<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 145 0 R
/T (MODEL 3: XGBOOST)
/E (MODEL 3: XGBOOST)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
284 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (XGBoost \(Extreme Gradient Boosting\) is an ensemble model that builds a sequence of decision trees, where each new tree corrects the errors of the previous ones. It was selected for its strong performance on structured/tabular healthcare data and its ability to model complex, non-linear relationships between features without requiring feature scaling. Sample weighting was applied during training to address class imbalance, ensuring the model didn't disproportionately favor the majority "failure" class. XGBoost also offers feature importance scores, providing interpretability into which clinical factors most influence treatment outcomes.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
